1
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,650
This is Momo.

2
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,230
This is a teddy bear.

3
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:15,330
Two eyes.

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:16,520
Soft fur.

5
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:17,810
One is living.

6
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,090
One is not.

7
00:00:19,182 --> 00:00:19,892
Easy?

8
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:22,322
Then try the six things in our box.

9
00:00:22,682 --> 00:00:24,372
First, a practice round.

10
00:00:24,602 --> 00:00:25,612
The teddy bear.

11
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:27,162
Point left for living.

12
00:00:27,382 --> 00:00:28,992
Point right for non-living.

13
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:29,912
Go!

14
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:36,318
Locked in!

15
00:00:36,448 --> 00:00:37,518
Non-living.

16
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:39,078
It never eats.

17
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:40,002
Non-living!

18
00:00:40,152 --> 00:00:41,472
It's full of cotton.

19
00:00:41,528 --> 00:00:43,508
But it has eyes and fur like me.

20
00:00:43,588 --> 00:00:45,018
Why isn't it living?

21
00:00:45,221 --> 00:00:47,411
The teddy bear is a non-living thing.

22
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,751
Eyes and fur are only how it looks.

23
00:00:49,971 --> 00:00:51,471
We need better clues.

24
00:00:51,981 --> 00:00:53,101
Here is the game.

25
00:00:53,321 --> 00:00:54,881
It's You against the Buddies.

26
00:00:55,091 --> 00:00:56,391
You lock in first.

27
00:00:56,611 --> 00:00:58,831
Then Pip, Basil and Momo answer.

28
00:00:58,953 --> 00:01:01,843
Every time you are right, put up one finger on your other

29
00:01:01,593 --> 00:01:02,283
hand.

30
00:01:02,513 --> 00:01:04,233
No lock-in, no point.

31
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:06,663
And a lizard is hiding in this video.

32
00:01:06,893 --> 00:01:07,723
Find it!

33
00:01:12,584 --> 00:01:14,284
Our six things came from here.

34
00:01:14,494 --> 00:01:17,094
A void deck and a garden in Toa Payoh.

35
00:01:17,324 --> 00:01:18,334
Look around.

36
00:01:18,455 --> 00:01:19,165
A mynah.

37
00:01:19,495 --> 00:01:20,275
Ants.

38
00:01:20,475 --> 00:01:21,705
A papaya tree.

39
00:01:21,925 --> 00:01:22,755
A bench.

40
00:01:22,975 --> 00:01:23,935
A bicycle.

41
00:01:24,165 --> 00:01:25,655
A blue recycling bin.

42
00:01:25,885 --> 00:01:27,325
So many different things!

43
00:01:27,987 --> 00:01:29,197
Say it with me!

44
00:01:29,908 --> 00:01:33,958
There is a great variety of living and non-living things around us.

45
00:01:34,188 --> 00:01:35,798
This is called diversity.

46
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:42,089
So many!

47
00:01:42,279 --> 00:01:43,629
How do we keep track?

48
00:01:43,641 --> 00:01:45,191
Let's start off with six.

49
00:01:45,411 --> 00:01:48,381
Let's put them into our glass box, and bring them back.

50
00:01:50,353 --> 00:01:51,273
Are you ready?

51
00:01:51,693 --> 00:01:52,453
Three!

52
00:01:52,843 --> 00:01:53,483
Two!

53
00:01:53,853 --> 00:01:54,483
One!

54
00:01:54,883 --> 00:01:55,553
Go!

55
00:01:56,351 --> 00:01:57,211
Day one.

56
00:01:57,511 --> 00:01:59,141
Six things, one box.

57
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:01,731
The lid has holes, so air can get in.

58
00:02:02,001 --> 00:02:05,621
The mealworm has oats to eat, and a juicy carrot for water.

59
00:02:05,881 --> 00:02:09,171
The plant has moist soil, and sunlight from the window.

60
00:02:10,943 --> 00:02:11,813
Round one.

61
00:02:12,053 --> 00:02:13,633
The wind-up robot.

62
00:02:13,873 --> 00:02:14,943
Look at it go!

63
00:02:15,153 --> 00:02:16,503
Point left for living.

64
00:02:16,703 --> 00:02:18,343
Point right for non-living.

65
00:02:23,818 --> 00:02:24,768
Locked in!

66
00:02:24,898 --> 00:02:25,598
Living!

67
00:02:25,718 --> 00:02:27,228
It moves, so it's living!

68
00:02:27,277 --> 00:02:28,337
Non-living.

69
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,527
I saw you wind it up, Basil.

70
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:31,560
Non-living.

71
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:33,220
Does it ever get hungry?

72
00:02:33,721 --> 00:02:34,501
Watch.

73
00:02:34,721 --> 00:02:36,041
The robot stops.

74
00:02:36,251 --> 00:02:38,101
A spring inside was pushing it.

75
00:02:38,235 --> 00:02:40,705
Nobody winds it up, so it stays still.

76
00:02:40,935 --> 00:02:41,845
All night.

77
00:02:42,065 --> 00:02:43,205
All of day two.

78
00:02:43,633 --> 00:02:45,973
It does not need water, food or air.

79
00:02:46,203 --> 00:02:47,383
It does not grow.

80
00:02:47,593 --> 00:02:50,273
The wind-up robot is a non-living thing.

81
00:02:50,937 --> 00:02:51,977
Pointed right?

82
00:02:52,197 --> 00:02:53,357
One finger up!

83
00:02:53,486 --> 00:02:54,066
Aww.

84
00:02:54,266 --> 00:02:55,866
So moving is not the clue!

85
00:02:55,916 --> 00:02:58,786
Then is a thing that stays still always non-living?

86
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:01,090
Round two.

87
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:02,200
Day two.

88
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:03,500
The green bean.

89
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:04,800
It is a seed.

90
00:03:05,050 --> 00:03:06,550
It has not moved at all.

91
00:03:06,810 --> 00:03:08,350
Living, or non-living?

92
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,370
Point!

93
00:03:14,837 --> 00:03:15,787
Locked in!

94
00:03:15,917 --> 00:03:16,987
Non-living.

95
00:03:17,207 --> 00:03:19,057
I watched it for one whole day.

96
00:03:19,307 --> 00:03:20,507
It did nothing.

97
00:03:20,555 --> 00:03:21,375
Living!

98
00:03:21,485 --> 00:03:23,085
It's green, like a leaf.

99
00:03:23,133 --> 00:03:23,833
Living!

100
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:26,013
Bean sprouts grow from green beans.

101
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:27,443
I eat bean sprouts!

102
00:03:27,871 --> 00:03:29,611
Three buddies, two answers.

103
00:03:29,831 --> 00:03:31,461
Let's shrink down and watch.

104
00:03:31,681 --> 00:03:32,541
Quietly.

105
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:37,126
You are tiny now.

106
00:03:37,406 --> 00:03:39,646
The green bean is as big as a bus.

107
00:03:41,058 --> 00:03:41,848
Listen.

108
00:03:45,296 --> 00:03:46,546
The skin splits.

109
00:03:46,826 --> 00:03:48,246
A root pushes out.

110
00:03:50,356 --> 00:03:51,866
Nobody wound it up.

111
00:03:52,156 --> 00:03:53,486
Nobody pushed it.

112
00:03:53,756 --> 00:03:55,526
It is growing by itself.

113
00:03:57,941 --> 00:03:59,881
The green bean is a living thing.

114
00:04:00,121 --> 00:04:01,621
It was living all along.

115
00:04:01,861 --> 00:04:02,941
It took in water.

116
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:04,641
Then it began to grow.

117
00:04:05,365 --> 00:04:06,445
Pointed left?

118
00:04:06,665 --> 00:04:07,825
One finger up!

119
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:09,110
I was careful.

120
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:11,310
But I did not watch long enough.

121
00:04:11,432 --> 00:04:13,152
Momo, living is right.

122
00:04:13,352 --> 00:04:15,262
But green is only how it looks.

123
00:04:15,492 --> 00:04:17,462
A green pencil is non-living.

124
00:04:17,522 --> 00:04:18,772
No point for me!

125
00:04:18,922 --> 00:04:20,342
So what ARE the clues?

126
00:04:21,216 --> 00:04:22,576
Did you spot the lizard?

127
00:04:22,816 --> 00:04:25,156
It was on the window at night, on day one.

128
00:04:25,386 --> 00:04:27,486
Is a lizard living or non-living?

129
00:04:27,686 --> 00:04:28,966
Tell someone at home.

130
00:04:29,995 --> 00:04:32,425
Our box has twenty-five more days to go.

131
00:04:32,645 --> 00:04:34,635
What will be under the cloth on Day thirty?

132
00:04:34,865 --> 00:04:36,345
Find out in Part Two!

133
00:04:37,219 --> 00:04:38,629
Show me your score hand!

134
00:04:40,106 --> 00:04:42,266
Let's read today's key words together!

135
00:04:42,506 --> 00:04:43,226
Ready?

136
00:04:43,566 --> 00:04:44,370
Diversity.

137
00:04:44,528 --> 00:04:45,564
Diversity.

138
00:04:46,114 --> 00:04:47,194
Living things.

139
00:04:47,212 --> 00:04:48,310
Living things.

140
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,140
Non-living things.

141
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:51,476
Non-living things.

142
00:04:52,026 --> 00:04:52,926
Well done!

143
00:04:53,909 --> 00:04:54,970
Say it with us!

144
00:04:55,770 --> 00:04:56,480
Ready?

145
00:04:56,605 --> 00:04:57,225
One!

146
00:04:57,605 --> 00:04:58,285
Two!

147
00:04:58,610 --> 00:04:59,785
Now you know!

148
00:04:58,610 --> 00:04:59,785
Now you know!
